    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.base16\n\n### Description\n\nmini.base16 overrides terminal colors with a supplied palette, which results in different colors in a neovim terminal than the ones configured in a terminal emulator:\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/94578451/040626eb-10ce-4c0f-ba92-547e052377c8)\r\nWhat is the reason for this? I believe there should at least be an option to turn this behavior off, as I found it jarring: neovim terminal isn't expected to have its own colors",
