    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What is the reason for this? I believe there should at least be an option to turn this behavior off, as I found it jarring: neovim terminal isn't expected to have its own colors\r\n\r\nThe reason for this is because I believe every buffer inside Neovim is expected to use colors from color scheme. If you don't want them, I'd suggest unsetting [`vim.g.terminal_color_x`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e94945129780fa5b43447ecc0a4b0273892043e3/lua/mini/base16.lua#L1190-L1205) variables. Like `vim.g.terminal_color_0 = nil`, and make sure to do that *after* `require('mini.base16').setup()`.\r\n\r\nClosing as both \"works as expected\" and \"not planned\".",
            "created_at": "2024-05-22T07:36:29Z",
